  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has an array AAA containing NNN non-negative integers.\n\nHe will perform a sequence of operations on this array.\n\nThe XXX-th operation is as follows:\n\n\nFor each index iii (1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N), either leave AiA_iAi​ unchanged, or replace AiA_iAi​ with Ai∣XA_i \\mid XAi​∣X.\n\nThe choice is made independently for each index.\n\nHere, ∣\\mid∣ denotes the bitwise OR operation.\nFind the minimum number of operations needed for Chef to be able to obtain an array that's sorted in non-decreasing order, i.e. for\n\nA1≤A2≤…≤ANA_1 \\leq A_2 \\leq\\ldots\\leq A_NA1​≤A2​≤…≤AN​ to hold.\n\nIt can be proved that the answer is finite.\n\nIf the array is already sorted, output 000.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum number of operations needed to obtain a sorted array.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤Ai≤1090 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^90≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3\n2 1 3\n4\n2 5 5 7\n5\n9 8 9 15 14",
        "output": "2\n0\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: One optimal sequence of operations is as follows.\n\nInitially, A=[2,1,3]A = [2, 1, 3]A=[2,1,3].\nFirst, we have X=1X = 1X=1.\nLeave all elements unchanged, so that A=[2,1,3]A = [2, 1, 3]A=[2,1,3] still.\nNext, we have X=2X = 2X=2.\nLeave A1A_1A1​ and A3A_3A3​ unchanged, and replace A2A_2A2​ by A2∣XA_2 \\mid XA2​∣X.\nThis will make the array [2,3,3][2, 3, 3][2,3,3], which is sorted.\n\nTest case 222: The array is already sorted.\nTest case 333: A=[9,8,9,15,14]A = [9, 8, 9, 15, 14]A=[9,8,9,15,14].\nFor X=1X = 1X=1, replace A2A_2A2​ and A5A_5A5​ by their bitwise ORs with XXX, to obtain [9,9,9,15,15][9, 9, 9, 15, 15][9,9,9,15,15] which is sorted."
      }
    ]
